/-!
# Common compactness on every fixed finite Fourier observation

This module forms the actual family of Galerkin trajectories generated by
all finite source paths satisfying one common strict critical margin.  On an
arbitrary fixed finite set of observed Fourier modes it proves:

* a cutoff-independent coefficient bound;
* a common `1 / 2`-Hölder modulus generated by the actual `H⁻¹` tangent
  budget; and
* compactness of the uniform closure by Arzelà--Ascoli.

The observed inventory need not be contained in any generated support.
Rows outside an individual support vanish by that trajectory's generated
physical law.  No trajectory, equicontinuity witness, compactness witness,
support-coverage hypothesis, or target limit occurs in the family mouth.
-/

